course: dictionary
lesson: 7565
title: Prescribe: what the doctor decides
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When a doctor prescribes a medicine, they officially say which medicine you should take, how much, and how often. «Medicine prescribed for one person is only for that person.» The word is about a decision made by someone who is allowed to make it.
explain: Prescribe can also mean to set an official rule. «The rules prescribe a uniform» means the rules say exactly what you must wear. Look at the clues around the word: a doctor, a dose or a rule tells you which meaning is in use.
explain: Look for the phrases that go with it: «prescribed dose», «as prescribed» and «prescribed by law». «Take the course exactly as prescribed» means follow the doctor's instructions exactly, not your own idea.
explain: In a maths problem, a doctor might prescribe «2 tablets, 3 times a day for 5 days». Multiply 2 × 3 × 5 to find the total: 30 tablets. The numbers in the problem are your clues.
fact: Prescribe means to say officially what should be done.
fact: A doctor prescribes a medicine by saying which one you should take, how much, and how often.
fact: A «prescribed dose» is the amount the doctor has officially said you should take.
fact: Only a doctor can prescribe certain medicines, and you must never take medicine prescribed for someone else.
fact: «Side effects» are unwanted effects on top of the ones you want from a medicine.
exercise: «A doctor prescribes two tablets a day.» What does prescribes mean here? | Makes a cup of tea for the patient | *Officially says which medicine to take, how much and how often | Sells the medicine in a shop
exercise: «The rules prescribe a uniform.» What does prescribe mean in this sentence? | *To say officially what must be worn | To forget the rules | To choose a colour for the school walls | To wash the uniform
exercise: Why must you never take medicine prescribed for someone else? | It tastes horrible | *It was chosen for their illness, age and weight, not yours | It is only for holidays | It is always too cheap
test: A doctor prescribes «2 tablets, 3 times a day for 5 days». How many tablets in total? | 60 | *30 | 25 | 15
test: «Take the course exactly as prescribed.» What does as prescribed mean? | *Exactly as the doctor has officially said | Only on Sundays | Whenever you feel like it | With a friend's medicine
exam: Which sentence uses prescribe to mean to set an official rule? | *The club rules prescribe a helmet for every rider | Our dog will prescribe the walk for today | Leo was tired and went straight to bed | The doctor will prescribe a cream for the rash
